+ Troubleshooting & Best Practices', '{"Day": "Day 21", "Week": "Week 5", "Topic": "Components, Props, State, Hooks\n+ Troubleshooting & Best Practices", "Module": "React", "Sub Topic": "Component decomposition for complete business journeys rather than isolated widgets\nReusable page shells, cards, forms, feedback components and loading/error components\nAdvanced props composition and event propagation across multiple levels\nState lifting vs state colocation across catalog, cart and account flows\nReusable custom hooks for common UI/session behaviors\nConsistent responsive behavior across the complete web journey\nAccessibility-aware component structure and keyboard-friendly interactions\nIntegration of routing, forms, state and reusable components into one cohesive React experience\nTroubleshooting & Best Practices – React:\n• Debugging with React DevTools: component tree, props/state inspection and Profiler\n• Troubleshooting common React issues: infinite re-render loops, stale closures, useEffect dependency bugs, missing keys, state not updating, routing/404 issues\n• Error boundaries and fallback UI for runtime errors\n• Best practices: feature-based folder structure, component/hook naming, avoiding prop drilling, immutable state updates, rules-of-hooks linting and a code-review checklist", "Hands-on Labs": "Case Study – React Web Journey Consolidation\nInput: Existing PulseCart catalog, product, cart and account pages from prior React sessions.\nImplement: Refactor the journey into reusable components and custom hooks; standardize state ownership and responsive behavior.\nIntegrate: Combine routing, forms, shared state and reusable UI into one cohesive multi-page React journey.\nValidate: Verify desktop/tablet/mobile behavior, navigation continuity, state preservation and component reuse.\nOutput: Consolidated React web user journey with reusable components and consistent interaction patterns.\nEvidence: Source code, screenshots across breakpoints, component map and short implementation note.", "Duration (Hrs)": "4", "Learning Outcomes": "Consolidate a complete React web journey using reusable components, hooks, routing and shared state without creating a separate lab day.", "Learning Type (SPL / IL)": "SPL"}'),
